    "fix": "Check you actually replaced the sample EXAMPLE_POSTS in persona.py with real posts you've written - the samples are placeholders, and the AI has no way to learn your specific voice from generic instructions alone. Real examples teach the model far more than adjectives do."
  },
  {
    "issue": "A post keeps getting flagged [CONTAINS CLICHE - REVIEW BEFORE POSTING]",
    "fix": "This is the guard working as designed, not a bug - the AI used a phrase persona.py explicitly bans. Either edit the post by hand in the Streamlit UI before saving, or regenerate; models are non-deterministic; a second attempt often avoids the same phrase."
  },
  {
    "issue": "Streamlit shows old post text after clicking Generate again",
    "fix": "Each text area uses a key tied to its post type (e.g. edit_INSIGHT), which is what lets your in-progress edits survive Streamlit's reruns - but it also means a second Generate click updates st.session_state['posts'] while the text areas may still show your last edits until you refresh. Reload the page if you want a fully clean slate."
  },
  {
    "issue": "save_posts() overwrites a file from earlier the same day",
    "fix": "Filenames are date-based (YYYYMMDD), not time-based, so saving the same post type twice in one day intentionally overwrites - that's the 'approved final version' for that day. If you want multiple drafts kept per day, add a time component to the filename in save_posts.py."
  }
